# .env.example — every knob a closed network (self-hosted GitLab, no direct
# internet, corporate proxy + internal mirrors) needs, with examples.
#
#   cp .env.example .env        # .env is gitignored; the `wt` helper copies it
#                               # into new worktrees
#
# Who reads .env:
#   • just      — `set dotenv-load` in the root justfile, so every recipe
#                 (go, docker build, docker compose, scanners) sees it
#   • mise      — `[env] _.file = ".env"` in mise.toml, so the mise shims
#                 (go, golangci-lint, …) see it even outside `just`
#   • CI        — nothing; set the same names as group/project CI variables
#                 (GitLab) or repository/organisation variables (GitHub). The
#                 pipelines only declare defaults, they never hard-code hosts.
#
# Everything below is commented out: the defaults are the public upstreams, so
# an open-network clone needs no .env at all. Uncomment what your network needs.

# ── Outbound HTTP proxy ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Honoured by go, git, curl, pnpm, mise, docker build (pass-through build args)
# and the docker daemon / dind service for image pulls.
#HTTP_PROXY=http://proxy.internal:3128
#HTTPS_PROXY=http://proxy.internal:3128
#NO_PROXY=localhost,127.0.0.1,::1,.internal,.svc,.cluster.local
# Lower-case twins for tools that only read these (curl, some Python tooling).
#http_proxy=http://proxy.internal:3128
#https_proxy=http://proxy.internal:3128
#no_proxy=localhost,127.0.0.1,::1,.internal,.svc,.cluster.local

# ── Go modules ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Module proxy. Athens, Nexus, Artifactory and the GitLab Package Registry
# (Go module proxy, per project) all speak the GOPROXY protocol. Keep `,direct`
# off in a closed network so a miss fails loudly instead of hanging on the
# proxy timeout.
#GOPROXY=https://goproxy.internal
#GOPROXY=https://gitlab.internal/api/v4/projects/<id>/packages/go
#
# Checksum database. Go first asks GOPROXY for /sumdb/sum.golang.org/supported;
# Athens / Nexus / Artifactory proxy the sumdb, so nothing to set with those.
# GitLab's Go proxy does not — then either exempt your private hosts
# (GONOSUMDB) or, last resort, disable verification (GOSUMDB=off).
#GONOSUMDB=gitlab.internal
#GOSUMDB=off
#
# Private module paths: skipped by the sumdb and fetched with git credentials.
#GOPRIVATE=gitlab.internal/*
#
# Never auto-download a newer toolchain (CI sets this too).
#GOTOOLCHAIN=local
#
# govulncheck's database. vuln.go.dev is a static site; mirror it with any
# HTTP server or rsync it to disk (file://).
#GOVULNDB=https://vulndb.internal
#GOVULNDB=file:///srv/mirrors/vulndb

# ── Container registries ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One variable per upstream registry, used as the image prefix everywhere:
# Dockerfiles (`FROM ${DOCKER_HUB}/library/golang…`), docker compose files,
# `.gitlab-ci.yml` image:/services:. Point each at the pull-through cache for
# that upstream (Harbor proxy project, Nexus docker-proxy, GitLab Dependency
# Proxy for Docker Hub: $CI_DEPENDENCY_PROXY_GROUP_IMAGE_PREFIX).
#DOCKER_HUB=harbor.internal/dockerhub
#GHCR=harbor.internal/ghcr
#GCR=harbor.internal/gcr
#
# testcontainers-go prefixes every Docker Hub image it starts with this
# (postgres, valkey/valkey, confluentinc/confluent-local). Trailing slash.
#TESTCONTAINERS_HUB_IMAGE_NAME_PREFIX=harbor.internal/dockerhub/
# If the daemon is remote (dind, a shared VM) or not on /var/run/docker.sock
# (OrbStack, rootless Docker), testcontainers needs to be told:
#DOCKER_HOST=tcp://docker:2375
#DOCKER_HOST=unix:///Users/<you>/.orbstack/run/docker.sock
#TESTCONTAINERS_RYUK_DISABLED=true

# ── Vulnerability databases (scanners) ────────────────────────────────────────
# grype: mirror the listing + DB tarballs, or import one by hand
# (`grype db import grype-db.tar.gz`) and switch auto-update off.
#GRYPE_DB_UPDATE_URL=https://mirror.internal/grype/listing.json
#GRYPE_DB_AUTO_UPDATE=false
#GRYPE_DB_VALIDATE_AGE=false
#
# osv-scanner: fetch the offline databases once on a connected host
# (`osv-scanner scan --offline --download-offline-databases …`), ship the
# directory, then point the scanner at it. Consumed by `just sec-deps` and the
# GitLab `dependency-scanning` job.
#OSV_SCANNER_FLAGS=--offline --local-db-path /srv/mirrors/osv
#
# semgrep: `p/…` packs are fetched from semgrep.dev. Vendor the rules
# (`semgrep --config p/golang --dump-config > semgrep/rules/golang.yml` on a
# connected host) and point here at the directory. Space-separated list.
#SEMGREP_CONFIG=semgrep/rules
# Also stops semgrep phoning home (the recipes pass --metrics=off already).
#SEMGREP_SEND_METRICS=off

# ── Node / pnpm (e2e + lefthook) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# `registry=` in .npmrc does the same for pnpm; corepack needs its own variable
# because it fetches pnpm itself before .npmrc is consulted.
#npm_config_registry=https://npm.internal
#COREPACK_NPM_REGISTRY=https://npm.internal
# Node tarballs (the GitLab allure-report job runs on a JRE image and adds Node).
#NODE_DIST_URL=https://mirror.internal/nodejs/dist

# ── Service runtime (per-service prefix: PING_ / HEARTBEAT_ / TASKS_ / CONSUMER_)
# Read by libs/httpx.LoadConfig in every binary; `just up` and the e2e harness
# forward .env to the processes they spawn, docker/stack.yml takes them as
# compose variables. Shown for tasks; the same three exist for each prefix.
# Bearer token for PUT/DELETE /admin/log-level on the admin listener
# (default "": mutations open — fine on localhost, not where the admin port
# is reachable by anyone else).
#TASKS_ADMIN_TOKEN=change-me
# Value of the X-Debug-Token request header that turns on debug logging for
# that one request, whatever the level (default "": the feature is off).
#TASKS_DEBUG_TOKEN=change-me
# Cap on how long a runtime log-level change (PUT /admin/log-level ?ttl=) can
# last before it reverts to the configured level (default 24h).
#TASKS_LOG_LEVEL_MAX_TTL=24h

# ── Image signing (cosign, key mode) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# `just docker-sign` reads the private key from the environment (env://); the
# public half is committed as cosign.pub for `just docker-verify`. Generate
# with `cosign generate-key-pair`, keep the key out of git (cosign.key is
# ignored) and in CI as a masked variable. Multi-line PEM: keep the quotes.
#COSIGN_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN ENCRYPTED SIGSTORE PRIVATE KEY-----
#…
#-----END ENCRYPTED SIGSTORE PRIVATE KEY-----"
# Passphrase of that key, so signing does not prompt (default: prompts).
#COSIGN_PASSWORD=

# ── mise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Most non-Go tools (gitleaks, hadolint, syft, grype, cosign) are GitHub
# release downloads and semgrep comes from PyPI — mise follows HTTPS_PROXY for
# all of them. Without any egress, run them as pinned images instead (the way
# .gitlab-ci.yml already does); see README "Closed networks".
#MISE_GITHUB_API_TOKEN=ghp_…
#PIP_INDEX_URL=https://pypi.internal/simple
